   "id": "q1",
   "objective": "Conditional types 0–III",
   "family": "q1",
   "type": "explain",
   "track": "explain",
   "prompt": "Read: the conditional types",
   "solution": "Type 0: If + present simple, present simple – always true (If you touch a fire, you get burnt). Type I: If + present simple, will + verb – possible/probable (If it rains, I will stay in). Type II: If + past simple, would/could + verb – improbable/unreal now (If I had a lot of money, I would travel). Type III: If + past perfect, would/could have + past participle – impossible, too late (If Napoleon had not invaded Russia, he would have stayed in power longer). Never use will/would in the if-clause – except polite requests.",
   "rubric": "Lesen und verstehen.",
   "sourceTitle": "Moodle EN · Conditional sentences",
   "sourceQuote": "Conditional types 0–III",
   "page": 1,
   "seconds": 45,
